 the build plate is integrally joined in freeform builds, it can be advantageous for use as tooling later in the process.
2.3.2. DEPOSITION HEAD AND SYSTEM OVERVIEW
The LP-DED system is made up of the deposition head, a laser energy source and optics, powder injection and shielding gas systems, and a motion control system (Fig. 2.40). Ancillary systems such as inert-gas flow systems, closed-loop control and monitoring, enclosures, and dust collectors are also incorporated in many DED systems. The deposition head is the core of the LP-DED process. The configuration of the deposition head may vary depending on the manufacturer. In some configurations, the optics are located within the deposition head, whereas in others, the head is attached to the laser optics. The deposition head’s primary function is injection of the powder into the focused laser beam to create the melt pool and deposit metal. The collimating, focal, and beam-shaping planes of the optics can allow for variations in the size and shape of the spot size. Variations specific to the motion control, powder injection, and environment exist, as shown in Fig. 2.41 and described in this section.
