2.3.3.1. LASER POWER
Laser power is the amount of thermal energy being introduced into the melt pool by the laser beam. It is controlled by the laser energy source and measured in watts and distributed over the area of the focusing spot size. Although the power is controlled by the energy source, some losses occur in the fiber-optic cable and the optics in the head that must be taken into account. The power density is a function of the laser power and melt-pool area, which is also defined by spot size. The laser power can be varied to increase or decrease the build rate, but the spot size must
