2.3.9. COMMON FAILURES FROM THE DED PROCESS
For the LP-DED process, visual observations can provide significant information on the parameters and health of the process. DED is much more akin to a typical welding process; visual, acoustic, and thermal monitoring techniques can be employed for in-process monitoring. If the process parameters have been optimized properly, the AM part build will generally be successful with a geometry that is feasible to fabricate given process constraints. If issues arise during the build, they will generally become apparent through excessive local deposition,
