3.6. CHALLENGES IN METAL AM
Despite the continued maturation of the different AM processes, several challenges still need to be addressed for metals. It is stressed throughout this book that the microstructure resulting from AM processing is highly dependent on the build parameters along with the post-processing, specifically the heat treatments. The build parameters may include the laser power, scan speed, laser focus diameter (spot size), layer thickness, hatch spacing or distance, scan strategy, build direction, recoater speed, gas flow rate, and powder feed rate (for LP-DED). Each of these parameters is highly influential on the microstructure, properties, and ultimately part quality [58].
