One of the oldest and most frequently used methods for thermal expansion measurement is mechanical dilatometry. The displacement that results from a specimen as its temperature is increased is mechanically transmitted to a sensor located away from the heat source, yielding a plot of displacement against temperature from which the CTE can be calculated. The sensors used to detect the change in displacement can range from strain gauges to optical imaging techniques.
