Benefits
Radiography uses ionizing radiation (generally x-rays) to penetrate the part. X-rays are scattered and absorbed as they interact with the material, which results in a difference in energy and intensity on the other side of the part. Traditionally, x-rays were recorded with film, but it is now typical to use computed or digital radiography, which convert x-ray energy into a digital signal. The total amount of material through which the x-rays pass determines the resulting amount of photons and energy. Different thicknesses of material, the presence of
