One of the hurdles to incorporating AM components into a larger system such as a liquid rocket engine is joining those AM components to other traditionally manufactured parts. It is necessary to treat metallic AM components as a new material class, similar to castings or forgings. Due to their unique grain structures and metallurgy, AM components will weld differently than other classes of metals.
