6.1.3. OTHER FEEDSTOCKS
The metal feedstock is highly dependent on the AM process selected for a particular application, as discussed in Chapter 2. Wire is the other primary feedstock for metal AM used in laser wire directed energy deposition (LW-DED), arc-wire directed energy deposition (AW-DED), and electron beam wire directed energy deposition (EBW-DED) systems. Wire is desirable because of its ease of handling, cleanliness, and safety and because its use usually results in less waste during the AM build process. Another significant benefit of wire is that high deposition rates can be achieved, making AM practical for large structures in which fine features are not essential. Metal sheet feedstock is used in the ultrasonic additive manufacturing (UAM) process, which bonds thin sheets of metal in a combined additive –subtractive process. UAM requires specific sheet dimensions to be fabricated for use in this process. The solid-state additive friction stir deposition (AFS-D) process can make use of both powder and solid rod or bar stock as the feedstock to form large structures [3]. Binder jetting uses a powder feedstock, but it also requires a binder to hold the green part in shape prior to sintering operations.
