6.3.4.4. RHEOLOGY
The rheological, or flow, properties of metal powders are of interest not only for AM but also for various powder metallurgy processes. In AM, the powder needs to be spread uniformly across a build plate or fed through a feed system and blown into the melt pool and subsequent part, so it must have desirable flow properties. A combination of parameters affect the flowability of a given powder. A few of the important factors include the applied force or constraints, powder size distribution and amount of fines, morphology, and moisture levels.
