7.3.10. POWDER REMOVAL
For powder to be removed from the internal channels, cavities, plenums, and manifolds of an L-PBF component, both entrance and exit paths to these features are required on the as-built part, before AM post-processing steps. To reiterate, entry and exit ports must be available while the part is still attached to the build plate. This is necessary because wire-EDM and thermal processing can potentially transform the loose powder into a claylike substance or cause powder sintering, which renders powder removal impossible in most cases. An entrance path is needed for compressed air to push the powder, and an exit path is needed for the powder to exit freely or be suctioned out with a vacuum.
