The ease of hardware customization and complexity using L-PBF is often described with the phrase “complexity is free!” The reality is, if L-PBF is not implemented with enough foresight, the challenges and cost of NDE will increase. Small and/or complex features can be difficult to inspect. Fortunately, the same capabilities that enable design freedom in the functional features of the part can also alleviate inspection challenges. A seasoned AM engineer will anticipate the need to include inspection ports or other means of accessibility for NDE in the design or opt for simpler geometries rather than unnecessarily complex ones. For example, a surface can be inspected with dye penetrant only if it can be accessed to apply penetrant and developer assuming if it is visible for imaging. Eddy current uses a probe that must have access to the surface of interest to be
