7.3.14. THREADED FEATURES
Printing of threads is not recommended for L-PBF parts. Threads are fine features that, when printed, will contain surface-connected pores that cannot be removed during hot isostatic pressing (HIP). These pores will induce failure of the threads at loads well below standard design margins. The recommended approach is to print a small pilot hole, much smaller than the required threaded hole, that can be drilled out to a larger diameter and then tapped. Many of the alloys used for propulsion applications are high in hardness, which make them challenging to machine. These features should be evaluated with the machining experts to determine whether a starting hole closer to the final diameter is preferred.
