7.3.20. SCAN ORDER
The order in which features or parts are scanned (laser sinter path) during the build is important to the success of the parts and metallurgical characteristics. The scan order is a function of the directions of both the recoater blade and the gas flow, which are again machine-specific. The proper scan order must start on parts farthest downstream of the gas flow so that ejecta generated during the scan process flow downstream of the part and are not deposited in the region of a neighboring part that is scanned later, avoiding potential impurities that can cause issues such as oversized grain. Figures 7.33 and 7.34 show examples of appropriate part placement on different platforms, which have very similar build envelopes, different recoater blade, and gas flow directions.
