7.7.1. DISTINCTION BETWEEN TOPOLOGY OPTIMIZATION AND GENERATIVE DESIGN
The terms topology optimization and generative design are often used interchangeably , but there is a distinction. Topology optimization is a computational technique for refining the material distribution within an available design space. Although several methods are available, they essentially compute the prioritization of material based on user-defined objectives, boundary conditions, and constraints. The part geometry is then defined using this material prioritization scale. By this definition, topology optimization can be considered a subset of generative
