8.1. INTRODUCTION
The performances of components built by additive manufacturing (AM) can be characterized in many different ways. Here, AM component performance is defined as the end-use technical capability in an application (whether it satisfies the intended applications), programmatic requirements (whether it meets the required cost, schedule, and risk), and processing-performance metrics (whether it balances quality with economics). The key aspects of AM component performance include, but are not limited to: geometric repeatability, engineering function, material properties, mass, cost, production schedule, aesthetics, and part complexity. The design, build, and post-processing phases of hardware impact each of these areas, as highlighted throughout this chapter. The specific alloy, design approach, AM feedstock and process, post-processing, resulting properties, and certification approach all play critical roles in determining the performance of an AM part. Proper technical design encompasses many intertwined disciplines, including materials science, fluid mechanics, structural mechanics, fracture mechanics, thermal analysis, dynamics, electromagnetic analysis, and manufacturing. All of the process steps (described in preceding chapters) are vital to obtaining the desired performance characteristics for the component’s service application. Chapter 5 focuses on the post-processing techniques available to the engineer for meeting broad end goals but not necessarily for the purpose of specific service applications. These techniques are critical to ensuring that the desired performance is met. Thus, an effective engineer must be (at the very least) familiar with multiple disciplines to successfully produce high-performing components. Just as surface texture (roughness and waviness) is a major consideration for the performance of AM components in terms of fatigue life, flow resistance, and heat transfer, it is also important for mating surfaces. Surfaces often require final machining to achieve flatness, surface finish, or proper porting for leak-free
