at are frequently encountered in production. The plan also delineates roles and responsibilities of all parties, which is crucial, especially for large or complex projects and programs that may stretch across multiple organizations. Additionally, consistency across the program and clear delineation of roles takes on a heightened importance when the design and production entities are not the same. With each added layer of subtier vendor supporting design and production, the complexity increases, and the need for clearly defined roles, responsibilities, and requirements becomes more important.
