9.7.2. TRAINING
NASA-STD-6033 requires operators who are certified in accordance with an operator training and certification program that is documented in the EFCP. This ensures that AM operations are executed by personnel with the proper knowledge and skill sets to implement the applicable AM processes. This includes skills such as the operation of the AM machine and all related equipment and an understanding of all procedural controls in place. All personnel training and certification records are kept within the QMS. Proper personnel certification is considered foundational to the methodology of NASA-STD-6030 and must be established before any aerospace hardware is produced. In the early days of AM, it was common for quality to follow specific individuals as they moved from company to company. These experts knew exactly how to make the AM machines produce specific characteristics of a high-quality part. Unfortunately, not all of the other individuals working at the facility knew all of the “tips and tricks” that the expert knew, and as a result, part quality was observed to be variable over time. The intent of the training program is that the knowledge required to produce a qualified part will be institutionalized and repeatable over time regardless of personnel changeover. Another important function of the personnel training program is to clearly delineate roles and responsibilities associated with the different levels or types of certification identified by the EFCP. For example, it is important to prevent a nonqualified person from accessing and modifying a build file or a design engineer from entering the production facility and starting to use an additive machine that they have not been trained to use. These scenarios present risks to hardware integrity and risks to the health and safety of personnel, as well as financial or programmatic risk in damaging expensive equipment. Having a consistent framework for the training and certification of operators and personnel enables the necessary consistency over time. Common methods for personnel training are on-the-job training and certificate programs, performed by either the AM production facility or a third-party. Such methods are appropriate for producing qualified
