9.8.1.1. POWDER FEEDSTOCK REUSE
The reuse of metal powder feedstocks is a complex topic, and the NASA AM certification methodology does not prescribe a direct solution for reuse at this time. The reuse issue primarily relates to concerns with contamination through oxidation, combustion products, and handling, as well as concerns with changes in the powder size distribution altering the way the powder flows and packs within the machine, although other issues not yet identified give rise to a general concern for the unknown. The reuse effects are strongly related to the alloy chemistry, the type and quality of AM machine, and the severity of the duty cycle to which the powder is exposed. Although NASA-STD-6030 does not prescribe reuse requirements, it does require that metrics based on properties trials be set to define powder life cutoff. The primary objectives regarding reuse control in NASA-STD-6030 are appropriate for smaller systems that do not automatically recycle powder. This is based on the concept that a metric has been defined that reasonably tracks the use state of the feedstock. Relying on this defined metric assumes that test data are available at the defined end of life for that metric that demonstrate that the feedstock does not show degradation in build quality or material performance (Chapter 6). The current reuse requirements are as follows:
1. Metrics are defined for tracking the progression of feedstock reuse for each machine operated in accordance with the QMP. Metrics for tracking feedstock reuse include, but are not limited to, machine operation hours, the number of days the feedstock is present in the machine, the number of build operations, and a combination of such metrics.
2. Limits on feedstock reuse are defined and implemented based on metrics.
3. The performance of AM material produced from reused feedstock up to the defined limit of reuse is tested and substantiated through material characterization in the MPS, which ensures that the properties of the reused material are statistically equivalent.
