9.8.5.2. SURFACE TEXTURE AND DETAIL RESOLUTION
Evaluations of the surface texture and detail resolution of the AM process provide important information regarding the nominal process operation, as well as indications of off-nominal process deviations. Maintaining consistent quality of the surface texture and detail resolution is particularly critical for parts challenged by high-cycle fatigue (HCF) performance of as-built surfaces. NASA-STD-6030 and associated documents do not impose specific quality metrics for surface texture and detail resolution for the purposes of qualifying a material process.
