9.12. PART PRODUCTION CONTROLS
Once foundational process controls are in place and the design values are based on controlled processes, the next step is part production controls. In this section of the chapter, the bottom half of Fig. 9.4 and Fig. 9.5 are referenced. Many aspects of part production control remain unchanged from traditional part production controls, but several unique AM process controls are critical to certification. In this section, the focus is on part classification, PPPs (including preproduction articles), and the QPP.
9.12.1. DESIGN CONSIDERATIONS
