The effective thermal conductivities of lattice specimens have been simulated and measured using an experimental test apparatus based on a modification of ASTM 1225-04 as shown in Figure 10.23. It has been found that thermal conductivity is proportional to percent relative density but not necessarily to lattice topology or unit-cell size. Lattice effective thermal conductivity (k) was found to be proportional to rrel (solid-volume-dominated) and dependent more on a and t rather than topology as shown in Figure 10.24 [2]. The convective heat-transfer coefficient is inversely proportional to unit-cell size, as small unit cells have more surface area per unit volume.
