 predicted that the maturity of in situ alloying will result in the development of new alloys. Overall, in situ alloying has been shown to work in AM, both in hypereutectic alloys and, more recently, in precipitation-strengthened alloys. Additional work is needed to develop the in situ process to find its limitations, improve its reproducibility, and explore the new alloy space.
