APPENDIX A
Mechanical Properties of Select AM Alloys
INTRODUCTION
Mechanical properties were obtained from specified additive manufacturing (AM) processes and alloys as examples of AM material properties that are being matured. The processes included Laser Powder Bed Fusion (L-PBF) and Laser Powder Directed Energy Deposition (LP-DED). This list is not intended to cover all alloys or processes. The samples presented herein completed full heat treatments within the tables provided. Independent Nadcap certified test laboratories completed all mechanical testing according to ASTM E8, ASTM E21, and ASTM E606. All Hot Isostatic Pressing (HIP) operations followed the procedures in ASTM3301-18a. Tensile specimens were all fully machined surface condition. Fatigue specimens are fully machined and the gage section precision ground, unless noted to be “As-built” condition. This data is provided as typical averages across these sets of alloys in the specified processes for certain machine platforms. These should not be used as design values. Furthermore, the user is encouraged to confirm for any specific end use application considerations to cover variation that may exists across different feedstocks, machine platforms, heat treatments, testing labs, or other variations within the process.
