INTRODUCTION
Various thermal properties were tested on specified additive manufacturing (AM) processes and samples as examples of AM material properties that are being matured. The processes included Laser Powder Bed Fusion (L-PBF) and Laser Powder Directed Energy Deposition (LP-DED). This list is not intended to cover all alloys or processes. All samples presented herein completed full heat treatments within the tables provided. The measurement equipment is complaint to and in accordance with ASTM E1461, ASTM E2585, DIN EN 821-2, DIN 30905, ISO 22007-4, ISO 18755, ISO 13826; DIN EN 1159-2, etc. This data is provided as typical averages across these sets of alloys in the specified processes for certain machine platforms. A standard deviation (STD) is provided based on repeat tests and samples. These should not be used as design values. Furthermore, the user is encouraged to confirm for any specific end use application considerations to cover variation that may exists across different feedstocks, machine platforms, heat treatments, testing labs, or other variations within the process.
