3. THERMAL PROPERTY DATA OF SELECT WROUGHT ALLOYS
Thermophysical testing revealed that the AM alloys had slight differences in thermal conductivity compared to equivalent wrought counterparts with similar heat treatments. The AM specimens all completed HIP, but the appropriate heat treatment, such as solution or aging, were similar for wrought specimens. To ensure the thermal conductivity difference was not measurement error, selected wrought alloys were tested under identical conditions on the same equipment and the results are provided in the following tables. AM has many microstructural differences from wrought ones that includes solidification along the primary thermal gradient (same direction as thermophysical test direction) and the chemical compositions are often held to lower impurity requirement in AM than the wrought counterparts.
